248
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:55,648
and suggest that the cheaper version will

249
00:08:55,648 --> 00:08:56,472
take months.

250
00:08:56,652 --> 00:08:58,208
Sometimes that is true.

251
00:08:58,388 --> 00:09:01,502
Sometimes the dealer simply makes more on

252
00:09:01,502 --> 00:09:03,020
the expensive truck.

253
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:04,417
Ask other dealers,

254
00:09:04,417 --> 00:09:06,377
and ask about factory orders,

255
00:09:06,377 --> 00:09:08,946
before you accept a truck with options

256
00:09:08,946 --> 00:09:10,027
you do not need.

257
00:09:10,377 --> 00:09:11,609
Trick number five:

258
00:09:11,609 --> 00:09:13,047
the trade-in shuffle.

259
00:09:13,227 --> 00:09:15,206
You get a great discount on the

260
00:09:15,206 --> 00:09:17,122
new truck, but a low offer for

261
00:09:17,122 --> 00:09:17,952
your old one.

262
00:09:18,132 --> 00:09:20,315
Or a great offer for your trade,

263
00:09:20,315 --> 00:09:22,567
but no discount on the new truck.

264
00:09:22,747 --> 00:09:25,270
The dealer moves money between the two

265
00:09:25,270 --> 00:09:27,792
numbers so that the total profit stays

266
00:09:27,792 --> 00:09:28,390
