269
00:09:33,227 --> 00:09:34,678
Here is the twist.

270
00:09:34,858 --> 00:09:36,968
Your trade-in is a separate deal,

271
00:09:36,968 --> 00:09:39,014
and it can be priced separately.

272
00:09:39,194 --> 00:09:41,311
Before you visit the dealer,

273
00:09:41,311 --> 00:09:44,185
get offers for your current truck from

274
00:09:44,185 --> 00:09:47,133
other sources, such as other dealers or

275
00:09:47,133 --> 00:09:48,192
online buyers.

276
00:09:48,372 --> 00:09:50,006
Then you know what it is really

277
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:50,322
worth.

278
00:09:50,502 --> 00:09:53,358
If the dealer's trade-in offer is lower,

279
00:09:53,358 --> 00:09:55,214
you can sell it elsewhere,

280
00:09:55,214 --> 00:09:56,714
or ask them to match.

281
00:09:57,064 --> 00:09:59,323
A good habit is to negotiate the

282
00:09:59,323 --> 00:10:00,876
new truck price first,

283
00:10:00,876 --> 00:10:02,853
as if you had no trade-in at

284
00:10:02,853 --> 00:10:03,136
all.

285
00:10:03,316 --> 00:10:05,770
Once that price is agreed in writing,

286
00:10:05,770 --> 00:10:07,031
bring up the trade.

287
00:10:07,211 --> 00:10:09,497
That way, the dealer cannot hide a

288
00:10:09,497 --> 00:10:12,052
low trade value inside a big discount,

289
00:10:12,052 --> 00:10:13,666
or the other way around.

290
00:10:13,846 --> 00:10:15,964
Each number has to stand on its

291
00:10:15,964 --> 00:10:16,238
own.

292
00:10:16,588 --> 00:10:18,503
And watch for negative equity.

293
00:10:18,683 --> 00:10:20,680
If you owe more on your current

294
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:22,162
truck than it is worth,

295
00:10:22,162 --> 00:10:24,545
some dealers will roll that debt into

296
00:10:24,545 --> 00:10:25,382
the new loan.

297
00:10:25,562 --> 00:10:27,938
The new truck then starts its life

298
00:10:27,938 --> 00:10:29,335
already upside down.

299
00:10:29,515 --> 00:10:32,249
With seven-year loans becoming common,

300
00:10:32,249 --> 00:10:33,760
according to Edmunds,

301
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:36,565
this cycle can follow buyers from truck

302
00:10:36,565 --> 00:10:37,213
to truck.

303
00:10:37,393 --> 00:10:39,622
Always ask to see exactly how much

304
00:10:39,622 --> 00:10:41,654
of the old loan is being added.

305
00:10:42,004 --> 00:10:43,308
Trick number six:

306
00:10:43,308 --> 00:10:45,150
the finance office menu.

307
00:10:45,330 --> 00:10:47,037
After you agree on a price,

308
00:10:47,037 --> 00:10:49,187
you are taken to a separate office

309
00:10:49,187 --> 00:10:50,578
to sign the paperwork.

310
00:10:50,758 --> 00:10:53,791
This is where extra products are offered:

311
00:10:53,791 --> 00:10:56,602
extended warranties, protection plans,

312
00:10:56,602 --> 00:10:58,378
tire and wheel coverage,

313
00:10:58,378 --> 00:11:00,301
theft protection and more.

314
00:11:00,481 --> 00:11:01,781
Some can be useful.

315
00:11:01,961 --> 00:11:03,207
Many are expensive,

316
00:11:03,207 --> 00:11:05,305
and they are added to your loan.

317
00:11:05,655 --> 00:11:07,151
According to CarEdge,

318
00:11:07,151 --> 00:11:09,931
among the most common add-ons on quotes

319
00:11:09,931 --> 00:11:11,499
were protection plans,

320
00:11:11,499 --> 00:11:15,490
averaging one thousand four hundred ninety-four dollars,

321
00:11:15,490 --> 00:11:16,986
and theft protection,

322
00:11:16,986 --> 00:11:20,051
averaging seven hundred eighty-two dollars.

323
00:11:20,231 --> 00:11:22,344
Financed over seven years,

324
00:11:22,344 --> 00:11:25,920
every dollar of those products also collects

325
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:26,651
interest.

326
00:11:26,831 --> 00:11:29,769
A one thousand five hundred dollar plan

327
00:11:29,769 --> 00:11:32,029
can cost much more by the time

328
00:11:32,029 --> 00:11:33,310
the loan is paid.

329
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:36,519
Another finance office move is the interest

330
00:11:36,519 --> 00:11:37,317
rate markup.

331
00:11:37,497 --> 00:11:39,612
The lender may approve you at one

332
00:11:39,612 --> 00:11:41,791
rate, and the dealer can offer you

333
00:11:41,791 --> 00:11:44,098
a slightly higher rate and keep part

334
00:11:44,098 --> 00:11:45,252
of the difference.

335
00:11:45,432 --> 00:11:46,767
It is a common,

336
00:11:46,767 --> 00:11:48,102
legal practice.

337
00:11:48,282 --> 00:11:50,718
That is why getting a pre-approved loan

338
00:11:50,718 --> 00:11:52,841
from your own bank or credit union

339
00:11:52,841 --> 00:11:55,026
before you visit gives you a number

340
00:11:55,026 --> 00:11:55,713
to compare.

341
00:11:55,893 --> 00:11:57,751
If the dealer can beat it,

342
00:11:57,751 --> 00:11:58,180
great.

343
00:11:58,360 --> 00:12:00,589
If not, you use your own loan.

344
00:12:00,939 --> 00:12:02,297
Here is the twist.

345
00:12:02,477 --> 00:12:05,213
Many of these products are negotiable,

346
00:12:05,213 --> 00:12:07,301
and many can be bought later,

347
00:12:07,301 --> 00:12:09,246
often from other providers.

348
00:12:09,426 --> 00:12:11,325
You do not have to decide in

349
00:12:11,325 --> 00:12:12,614
the finance office,

350
00:12:12,614 --> 00:12:15,463
under pressure, after hours at the dealer.

351
00:12:15,643 --> 00:12:16,654
How to beat it:

352
00:12:16,654 --> 00:12:19,283
decide before you go which products you

353
00:12:19,283 --> 00:12:20,159
want, if any.

354
00:12:20,339 --> 00:12:22,324
Ask for the price of each product

355
00:12:22,324 --> 00:12:24,368
separately, and do not let them be

356
00:12:24,368 --> 00:12:26,353
bundled into the monthly payment.

357
00:12:26,703 --> 00:12:28,394
Trick number seven:

358
00:12:28,394 --> 00:12:29,106
urgency.

359
00:12:29,286 --> 00:12:31,120
This price is only good today.

360
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:33,616
Another buyer is coming to look at

361
00:12:33,616 --> 00:12:35,387
this truck this afternoon.

362
00:12:35,567 --> 00:12:38,411
My manager will only approve this once.

363
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:41,045
Urgency is designed to stop you from

364
00:12:41,045 --> 00:12:41,726
comparing.

365
00:12:41,906 --> 00:12:43,809
A buyer who leaves to think it

366
00:12:43,809 --> 00:12:46,284
over might find a better deal somewhere

367
00:12:46,284 --> 00:12:48,187
else, and the dealer knows it.

368
00:12:48,537 --> 00:12:49,825
Here is the twist.

369
00:12:50,005 --> 00:12:51,584
Comparing pays.

370
00:12:51,764 --> 00:12:53,319
According to CarEdge,

371
00:12:53,319 --> 00:12:57,170
buyers who compare out-the-door quotes from multiple

372
00:12:57,170 --> 00:12:59,762
dealers save an average of three to

373
00:12:59,762 --> 00:13:02,724
five percent off the first quoted price.

374
00:13:02,904 --> 00:13:06,013
On a truck that costs sixty-seven thousand

375
00:13:06,013 --> 00:13:09,419
dollars, the average full-size pickup price in

376
00:13:09,419 --> 00:13:13,268
September twenty twenty-six according to Kelley Blue

377
00:13:13,268 --> 00:13:16,007
Book, five percent is more than three

378
00:13:16,007 --> 00:13:17,266
thousand dollars.

379
00:13:17,616 --> 00:13:19,601
Urgency also shows up at the end

380
00:13:19,601 --> 00:13:21,214
of the month or the end of

381
00:13:21,214 --> 00:13:21,772
the year.

382
00:13:21,952 --> 00:13:24,193
Dealers often have sales targets,

383
00:13:24,193 --> 00:13:26,977
and they may genuinely offer better deals

384
00:13:26,977 --> 00:13:27,792
to hit them.

385
00:13:27,972 --> 00:13:30,080
That kind of urgency can work in

386
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:30,805
your favor.

387
00:13:30,985 --> 00:13:33,736
The trick is knowing the difference between

388
00:13:33,736 --> 00:13:36,104
real deadlines that help you and fake

389
00:13:36,104 --> 00:13:38,919
deadlines designed to stop you from shopping

390
00:13:38,919 --> 00:13:39,367
around.

391
00:13:39,717 --> 00:13:40,791
How to beat it:

392
00:13:40,791 --> 00:13:43,512
get written quotes from at least three

393
00:13:43,512 --> 00:13:45,661
dealers, by email if possible.

394
00:13:45,841 --> 00:13:48,778
A real price will still exist tomorrow.

395
00:13:48,958 --> 00:13:51,466
If the deal truly disappears overnight,

396
00:13:51,466 --> 00:13:53,394
it was probably not as good as

397
00:13:53,394 --> 00:13:54,101
it sounded.

398
00:13:54,281 --> 00:13:56,603
There are many trucks and many dealers.

399
00:13:56,783 --> 00:13:58,920
There is almost never only one.

400
00:13:59,270 --> 00:14:01,782
Now the twist that affects every buyer

401
00:14:01,782 --> 00:14:02,509
in America.

402
00:14:02,689 --> 00:14:04,242
In twenty twenty-four,

403
00:14:04,242 --> 00:14:07,207
the Federal Trade Commission created a new

404
00:14:07,207 --> 00:14:09,113
rule, called the CARS Rule,

405
00:14:09,113 --> 00:14:11,443
to fight many of these practices.

406
00:14:11,623 --> 00:14:13,705
According to ConsumerAffairs,

407
00:14:13,705 --> 00:14:16,720
it would have required dealers to disclose

408
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:18,946
the total vehicle cost upfront,

409
00:14:18,946 --> 00:14:21,243
state that add-ons are optional,

410
00:14:21,243 --> 00:14:24,115
and get consumer consent for extra fees.

411
00:14:24,465 --> 00:14:25,869
It never took effect.

412
00:14:26,049 --> 00:14:27,899
On January twenty-seventh,

413
00:14:27,899 --> 00:14:31,171
twenty twenty-five, the Fifth Circuit Court of

414
00:14:31,171 --> 00:14:33,518
Appeals vacated the rule in a two

415
00:14:33,518 --> 00:14:34,656
to one decision,

416
00:14:34,656 --> 00:14:37,786
after a challenge by the National Automobile

417
00:14:37,786 --> 00:14:41,485
Dealers Association and the Texas Automobile Dealers

418
00:14:41,485 --> 00:14:42,338
Association.

419
00:14:42,518 --> 00:14:44,411
The court said the F T C

420
00:14:44,411 --> 00:14:47,725
violated its own regulations by skipping a

421
00:14:47,725 --> 00:14:51,353
required early step in the rulemaking process.

422
00:14:51,704 --> 00:14:53,869
According to ConsumerAffairs,

423
00:14:53,869 --> 00:14:56,110
dealers are still at risk of F

424
00:14:56,110 --> 00:14:58,873
T C scrutiny for deceptive practices,

425
00:14:58,873 --> 00:15:01,711
and the agency could revisit the rule.

426
00:15:01,891 --> 00:15:02,652
But for now,

427
00:15:02,652 --> 00:15:05,189
the protections it promised are not law.

428
00:15:05,369 --> 00:15:08,495
That means the job of spotting add-ons,

429
00:15:08,495 --> 00:15:11,701
fees and pressure tactics still falls on

430
00:15:11,701 --> 00:15:12,904
you, the buyer.

431
00:15:13,084 --> 00:15:14,631
This video, in a way,

432
00:15:14,631 --> 00:15:16,915
is the rule that never arrived.

433
00:15:17,265 --> 00:15:19,796
And remember that good dealers exist.

434
00:15:19,976 --> 00:15:22,467
Many dealers publish clear prices,

435
00:15:22,467 --> 00:15:25,397
skip add-ons and charge reasonable fees.

436
00:15:25,577 --> 00:15:27,042
According to CarEdge,

437
00:15:27,042 --> 00:15:29,763
fifty-six percent of the dealers in its

438
00:15:29,763 --> 00:15:32,693
twenty twenty-six report earned an A grade

439
00:15:32,693 --> 00:15:33,739
for their fees.

440
00:15:33,919 --> 00:15:35,899
Your goal is not to fight every

441
00:15:35,899 --> 00:15:36,346
dealer.

442
00:15:36,526 --> 00:15:38,398
It is to find the honest ones,

443
00:15:38,398 --> 00:15:40,395
and the tools in this video make

444
00:15:40,395 --> 00:15:41,518
them easy to spot.

445
00:15:41,868 --> 00:15:43,372
Here is a bonus trick,

446
00:15:43,372 --> 00:15:45,629
because there is always one more.

447
00:15:45,809 --> 00:15:46,993
The spot delivery.

448
00:15:47,173 --> 00:15:49,384
You sign the papers and drive the

449
00:15:49,384 --> 00:15:52,131
truck home before the financing is final.

450
00:15:52,311 --> 00:15:54,967
Days later, the dealer calls to say

451
00:15:54,967 --> 00:15:57,471
the loan was not approved at that

452
00:15:57,471 --> 00:15:59,824
rate, and asks you to come back

453
00:15:59,824 --> 00:16:01,948
and sign a new contract at a

454
00:16:01,948 --> 00:16:02,783
higher one.

455
00:16:02,963 --> 00:16:04,455
Before you drive away,

456
00:16:04,455 --> 00:16:07,302
make sure the financing is fully approved,

457
00:16:07,302 --> 00:16:08,048
in writing.

458
00:16:08,399 --> 00:16:09,745
And a second bonus:

459
00:16:09,745 --> 00:16:11,162
the payment packing.

460
00:16:11,342 --> 00:16:14,874
A salesperson quotes a monthly payment that

461
00:16:14,874 --> 00:16:17,503
already includes extra products,

462
00:16:17,503 --> 00:16:18,981
without saying so.

463
00:16:19,161 --> 00:16:21,237
When you agree to the payment,

464
00:16:21,237 --> 00:16:24,281
you have unknowingly agreed to the products.

465
00:16:24,461 --> 00:16:26,981
The fix is the same as always.

466
00:16:27,161 --> 00:16:29,746
Ask for an itemized breakdown of the

467
00:16:29,746 --> 00:16:30,895
price, the fees,

468
00:16:30,895 --> 00:16:33,840
the products and the interest rate before

469
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,636
you agree to any payment.

470
00:16:35,986 --> 00:16:37,829
What can you do if something goes

471
00:16:37,829 --> 00:16:38,946
wrong after you buy?

472
00:16:39,126 --> 00:16:42,205
Keep copies of every document and every

473
00:16:42,205 --> 00:16:42,679
email.

474
00:16:42,859 --> 00:16:45,225
If you believe a dealer misled you,

475
00:16:45,225 --> 00:16:47,929
you can contact the dealer's management,

476
00:16:47,929 --> 00:16:50,362
the manufacturer's customer service,

477
00:16:50,362 --> 00:16:53,269
your state attorney general or the consumer

478
00:16:53,269 --> 00:16:55,432
protection office in your state.

479
00:16:55,612 --> 00:16:58,573
Documentation is what makes a complaint work.

480
00:16:58,923 --> 00:17:02,011
And remember that the paperwork rules everything.

481
00:17:02,191 --> 00:17:04,451
Whatever the salesperson promised,

482
00:17:04,451 --> 00:17:06,777
the signed contract is what counts.

483
00:17:06,957 --> 00:17:08,606
If a promise matters,

484
00:17:08,606 --> 00:17:10,333
like free maintenance,

485
00:17:10,333 --> 00:17:12,295
a second key or a repair,

486
00:17:12,295 --> 00:17:14,808
make sure it is written into the

487
00:17:14,808 --> 00:17:17,477
contract or a signed form called a

488
00:17:17,477 --> 00:17:18,184
due bill.

489
00:17:18,364 --> 00:17:21,184
A verbal promise disappears the moment you

490
00:17:21,184 --> 00:17:22,392
drive off the lot.

491
00:17:22,743 --> 00:17:24,919
So what do all seven tricks have

492
00:17:24,919 --> 00:17:25,599
in common?

493
00:17:25,779 --> 00:17:27,949
They move your attention away from the

494
00:17:27,949 --> 00:17:28,635
total price.

495
00:17:28,815 --> 00:17:31,833
The monthly payment hides the loan length.

496
00:17:32,013 --> 00:17:34,521
The add-on sticker hides extra profit.

497
00:17:34,701 --> 00:17:37,093
The doc fee hides in the paperwork.

498
00:17:37,273 --> 00:17:39,815
The trade-in shuffle hides in the math.

499
00:17:39,995 --> 00:17:42,329
And urgency hides the competition.

500
00:17:42,509 --> 00:17:44,792
Every trick works by making the total

501
00:17:44,792 --> 00:17:45,655
harder to see.

502
00:17:46,006 --> 00:17:48,479
And that is why one question beats

503
00:17:48,479 --> 00:17:51,462
all seven: what is my out-the-door price?

504
00:17:51,642 --> 00:17:53,068
Ask it in writing,

505
00:17:53,068 --> 00:17:54,731
from several dealers,

506
00:17:54,731 --> 00:17:57,187
before you talk about payments,

507
00:17:57,187 --> 00:17:58,771
trade-ins or extras.

508
00:17:58,951 --> 00:18:00,646
Everything else is detail.

509
00:18:00,826 --> 00:18:03,492
The buyer who controls the total controls

510
00:18:03,492 --> 00:18:04,077
the deal.

511
00:18:04,427 --> 00:18:06,625
And a final note on timing your

512
00:18:06,625 --> 00:18:07,050
visit.

513
00:18:07,230 --> 00:18:09,495
Dealers are busiest on weekends,

514
00:18:09,495 --> 00:18:13,174
when salespeople juggle several buyers and decisions

515
00:18:13,174 --> 00:18:13,953
are rushed.

516
00:18:14,133 --> 00:18:15,252
A weekday visit,

517
00:18:15,252 --> 00:18:18,259
with an appointment and your written quotes

518
00:18:18,259 --> 00:18:21,337
in hand, usually means a calmer conversation

519
00:18:21,337 --> 00:18:22,666
and more attention.

520
00:18:22,846 --> 00:18:25,470
A calm buyer makes better decisions.

521
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:27,433
Bring a friend if you can.

522
00:18:27,613 --> 00:18:30,148
A second person can notice things you

523
00:18:30,148 --> 00:18:32,272
miss, ask questions you forget,

524
00:18:32,272 --> 00:18:34,601
and remind you of your limits when

525
00:18:34,601 --> 00:18:35,903
the pressure rises.

526
00:18:36,083 --> 00:18:39,116
Many dealer tricks work because buyers are

527
00:18:39,116 --> 00:18:41,210
tired and alone at the end of

528
00:18:41,210 --> 00:18:42,004
a long day.

529
00:18:42,184 --> 00:18:44,216
Do not give them that advantage.

530
00:18:44,566 --> 00:18:46,446
One more tool that works:

531
00:18:46,446 --> 00:18:47,874
walk away politely.

532
00:18:48,054 --> 00:18:49,770
Thank the salesperson,

533
00:18:49,770 --> 00:18:51,642
leave your phone number,

534
00:18:51,642 --> 00:18:52,188
and go.

535
00:18:52,368 --> 00:18:55,038
Many buyers find that the best offer

536
00:18:55,038 --> 00:18:56,892
arrives after they leave,

537
00:18:56,892 --> 00:18:58,227
by phone or email,

538
00:18:58,227 --> 00:19:01,120
once the dealer realizes the sale might

539
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:01,714
be lost.

540
00:19:01,894 --> 00:19:04,134
Walking away is not rude.

541
00:19:04,314 --> 00:19:06,833
It is the strongest negotiating move a

542
00:19:06,833 --> 00:19:07,496
buyer has.

543
00:19:07,846 --> 00:19:09,715
And bring the numbers with you.

544
00:19:09,895 --> 00:19:12,753
Write down the out-the-door quotes from other

545
00:19:12,753 --> 00:19:15,420
dealers, the trade-in offers you received,

546
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:17,453
and your pre-approved loan rate.

547
00:19:17,633 --> 00:19:19,770
When a buyer shows up with real

548
00:19:19,770 --> 00:19:22,114
numbers, the conversation changes.

549
00:19:22,294 --> 00:19:24,407
It stops being about what you might

550
00:19:24,407 --> 00:19:26,941
accept, and starts being about whether the

551
00:19:26,941 --> 00:19:28,691
dealer can beat a real offer.

552
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:31,242
So here is your checklist for twenty

553
00:19:31,242 --> 00:19:32,037
twenty-seven.

554
00:19:32,217 --> 00:19:34,558
First, ask for the out-the-door price in

555
00:19:34,558 --> 00:19:35,027
writing.

556
00:19:35,207 --> 00:19:38,206
Second, ask for the price without dealer

557
00:19:38,206 --> 00:19:38,806
add-ons.

558
00:19:38,986 --> 00:19:41,772
Third, know your state's doc fee rules.

559
00:19:41,952 --> 00:19:45,191
Fourth, get your trade-in valued elsewhere first.

560
00:19:45,371 --> 00:19:48,279
And fifth, decide on any extra products

561
00:19:48,279 --> 00:19:50,963
before you enter the finance office,

562
00:19:50,963 --> 00:19:53,498
and never let them be bundled into

563
00:19:53,498 --> 00:19:54,392
the payment.

564
00:19:54,743 --> 00:19:56,400
We put the full version,

565
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:58,816
with the exact questions to ask and

566
00:19:58,816 --> 00:20:00,404
the numbers to compare,

567
00:20:00,404 --> 00:20:03,787
